 <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>]</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Fin\">Fin</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Data/Fin/Lemmas.html#Fin.intCast","kind":"def","line":135,"name":"Fin.intCast","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/11acb17ec6b07a8f9e9173e6845197929540936b/src/Init/Data/Fin/Lemmas.lean#L135-L139"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Fin/Lemmas.html#Fin.NatCast.instNatCast\"><span class=\"name\">Fin</span>.<span class=\"name\">NatCast</span>.<span class=\"name\">instNatCast</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">[<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/NeZero.html#NeZero\">NeZero</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>]</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Cast.html#NatCast\">NatCast</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Fin\">Fin</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span>)</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"This is not a global instance, but may be activated locally via `open Fin.NatCast in ...`.\n\nThis is not an instance because the `binop%` elaborator assumes that\nthere are no non-trivial coercion loops,\nbut this introduces a coercion from `Nat` to `Fin n` and back.\n\nNon-trivial loops lead to undesirable and counterintuitive elaboration behavior.\nFor example, for `x : Fin k` and `n : Nat`,\nit causes `x < n` to be elaborated as `x < ↑n` rather th